            'en' => [
                'title'   => 'Laser business ideas: 10 products you can make and sell',
                'slug'    => 'laser-business-ideas',
                'excerpt' => 'Personalised gifts, branded merchandise and industrial marking. Ideas for what to make with a laser and which equipment you will need.',
                'blocks'  => [
                    [ 'p', 'A laser turns inexpensive material into a personalised product that customers are happy to pay more for. Many small businesses start with one machine and a few proven products. Here are ten ideas that are easy to start with – and the type of laser each one needs.' ],
                    [ 'h2', 'Personalised gifts' ],
                    [ 'h3', '1. Cutting boards and kitchen accessories' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Names, dedications or family recipes engraved on wood are classic wedding and holiday gifts. Wood works very well with diode and CO₂ lasers.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '2. Jewellery and key rings' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Earrings, pendants and key rings cut from wood or acrylic, or engraved on ready-made steel blanks. Metal requires a fibre or MOPA laser.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '3. Engraved glass and crystal' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Wine glasses, tumblers and trophies with a name or logo. A CO₂ laser works on glass, and a UV laser creates 3D engravings inside crystal.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '4. Leather goods' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Wallets, belts, phone cases and key fobs with initials. Diode and CO₂ lasers engrave leather well.' ],
                    [ 'h2', 'For businesses and events' ],
                    [ 'h3', '5. Branded merchandise' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Pens, flasks, power banks and tools with a durable customer logo. Most of these products are made of metal, so you will need a fibre or MOPA laser – MOPA can also create colour marks on steel.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '6. Signs and labels' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Shop signs, door plates and office signage made of acrylic, wood or engraving laminate. A CO₂ laser is best for cutting acrylic.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '7. Awards and trophies' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Awards for companies, schools and sports clubs often combine several materials: acrylic, wood and metal. A machine that offers more than one type of laser is useful here.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '8. Invitations and decorations' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Lace-cut invitations, place cards and wedding decorations made of paper, card and thin plywood. These jobs are seasonal but often repeat.' ],
                    [ 'h2', 'Production and crafts' ],
                    [ 'h3', '9. Nameplates and part marking' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Serial numbers, QR codes and labels on metal parts must be durable and legible. This is a job for a fibre or MOPA laser.' ],
                    [ 'h3', '10. DIY kits and model making' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Precisely cut plywood and acrylic parts for assembly – from models and puzzles to organisers and lamps.' ],
                    [ 'h2', 'Which equipment to start with?' ],
                    [ 'p', 'A diode laser is enough for wood, leather and paper, while a CO₂ laser is the choice for fast acrylic cutting and larger batches. If you want to work with metal and glass, consider a machine with a MOPA or UV laser. The F2 is a Class 4 professional laser: xTool requires training and laser safety officer oversight and prohibits use in public or around untrained people or children.' ],
                    [ 'products', "$m2,$f2,$f2_uv" ],
                    [ 'h2', 'How to work out profitability' ],
                    [ 'p', 'Before you set prices, calculate the cost of material, machine time and your own time preparing the design. Personalisation is the added value: customers pay for a name, a date or a logo, not just for a piece of wood. Start with a few products, see what sells best and only then expand your range.' ],
                    [ 'ul', [
                        'Prepare design templates so that personalisation takes minutes.',
                        'Take good photos of finished products – they are what sells in an online shop and on social media.',
                        'Check the legal and tax requirements for running a business and selling before you start.',
                    ] ],
                    [ 'p', 'Not sure which laser suits your ideas? Book a demo – we will show you how the machines handle the materials you care about.' ],
                ],
            ],
            'de' => [
                'title'   => 'Geschäftsideen mit dem Laser: 10 Produkte, die Sie verkaufen können',
